---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConverterBar from '../components/ConverterBar.astro';
import InputPanel from '../components/InputPanel.astro';
import PreviewTable from '../components/PreviewTable.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="CSV to JSON Converter — Convert CSV to JSON Online Free" description="Convert CSV to JSON online free. Paste CSV data or upload a .csv file. Smart header detection, type inference, and nested object support. 100% browser-based." keywords="csv to json, csv to json converter, convert csv to json, csv to json online, csv to json free" breadcrumbs={[{name:'Home',url:'/'},{name:'CSV to JSON Converter',url:'/csv-to-json-converter'}]}>
  <main class="landing">
    <section class="landing-hero">
      <h1>CSV to JSON Converter</h1>
      <p class="landing-desc">Turn your CSV spreadsheets into clean JSON objects — instantly. Perfect for importing tabular data into APIs, databases, or JavaScript applications. Smart column typing and header detection built in.</p>
    </section>

    <ConverterBar from="CSV" to="JSON" />
    <InputPanel />
    <PreviewTable />

    <section class="landing-content">
      <h2>Why Convert CSV to JSON?</h2>
      <p>CSV is the lingua franca of spreadsheets and database exports, but JSON is what web APIs, NoSQL databases, and modern JavaScript/TypeScript applications consume natively. Converting CSV to JSON lets you take any tabular data — from bank statements to survey results — and use it directly in your application code.</p>
      <p>Typical scenarios include loading product inventory from an ERP spreadsheet into a headless CMS, importing customer lists from CSV exports into a Firebase or MongoDB collection, or preparing test fixtures from existing tabular data for unit tests.</p>

      <h2>How Rows Become JSON</h2>
      <p>Each row in the CSV becomes one JSON object. The first row provides the keys (column headers), and subsequent rows provide the values. For example:</p>
      <p><code>name,age,city<br>Alice,30,NYC<br>Bob,25,LA</code></p>
      <p>becomes:</p>
      <p><code>[&lbrace;"name":"Alice","age":30,"city":"NYC"&rbrace;,&lbrace;"name":"Bob","age":25,"city":"LA"&rbrace;]</code></p>
      <p>The converter detects column types automatically: quoted strings stay strings, unquoted numbers become numbers, and common date formats are preserved. Empty cells are included as <code>null</code> so downstream code can handle missing data explicitly.</p>

      <h2>How to Convert CSV to JSON</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Select <strong>CSV</strong> as source and <strong>JSON</strong> as target format</li>
        <li>Paste your CSV, upload a <code>.csv</code> file, or fetch from a URL</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Convert</strong> or press <kbd>Ctrl+Enter</kbd></li>
        <li>Preview the result, edit inline if needed, then download as JSON</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Features</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Detects column types: strings, numbers, booleans, dates</li>
        <li>First row is treated as headers for key names</li>
        <li>Output as array of objects (default) or array of arrays</li>
        <li>Preserves empty cells versus missing keys</li>
        <li>Inline editing, sorting, filtering before download</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common Use Cases</h2>
      <p><strong>API integration:</strong> Your partner sends a CSV of daily transactions. Convert to JSON and POST directly to your REST endpoint.</p>
      <p><strong>Database seeding:</strong> Export a reference table from MySQL as CSV, convert to JSON, and use it as seed data for MongoDB or a Firebase collection.</p>
      <p><strong>Frontend development:</strong> A designer provides data in a spreadsheet. Convert to JSON and import it directly into a React/Vue component's state or mock service worker.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .landing { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .landing-hero { text-align: center; padding: 40px 16px 24px; }
  .landing-hero h1 { font-size: 32px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.5px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .landing-desc { font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.7; }
  .landing-content { padding: 40px 16px 60px; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .landing-content h2 { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; margin: 32px 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.3px; }
  .landing-content p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .landing-content ul, .landing-content ol { padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .landing-content li { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .landing-content kbd { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 5px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .landing-hero h1 { font-size: 24px; }
    .landing-hero { padding: 24px 16px 16px; }
    .landing-content h2 { font-size: 18px; }
  }
</style>
